problem:
Determine whether there exists a polynomial \( f(x_1, x_2) \) with two variables and integer coefficients, and two points \( A = (a_1, a_2) \) and \( B = (b_1, b_2) \) in the plane, satisfying the following conditions:
(i) \( A \) is an integer point (i.e., \( a_1 \) and \( a_2 \) are integers);
(ii) \( |a_1 - b_1| + |a_2 - b_2| = 2010 \);
(iii) \( f(n_1, n_2) > f(a_1, a_2) \) for all integer points \( (n_1, n_2) \) in the plane other than \( A \);
(iv) \( f(x_1, x_2) > f(b_1, b_2) \) for all integer points \( (x_1, x_2) \) in the plane other than \( B \).

In a solitaire game, starting from a finite string of zeros and ones, the following moves are allowed:
(i) cancel each two consecutive ones;
(ii) delete three consecutive zeros;
(iii) if the substring within the string is $01$, one may replace this by substring $100$.
The moves must be made one at a time. You win if you can reduce the string to a string formed by two digits or less.
Among all the $1024$ possible strings of ten-digit binary numbers, how many are there from which it is not possible to win the solitaire?
